   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The quotient of consecutive terms is \\( r = - \\frac{x}{2} - 1 \\), the same for every n, so the series is geometric. Its first term is the \\( n = 2 \\) term, \\( a = 7 \\left(- \\frac{x}{2} - 1\\right)^{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            7,
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     -1,
                     [
                        "Rational",
                        1,
                        2
                     ],
                     "x"
                  ],
                  -1
               ],
               2
            ]
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99067",
         "rule_named": "first term and ratio"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "It converges when \\( |r| < 1 \\), that is for \\( \\left|x + 2\\right| < 2 \\).",
         "rule_named": "convergence condition"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "There the sum is \\( \\frac{a}{1 - r} = \\frac{7 \\left(x + 2\\right)^{2}}{2 \\left(x + 4\\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
